  "details": "## Problem\n\nCoordinating identical camera angles between multiple users is slow and imprecise. Creators, photographers, streamers, and event staff currently align by hand or exchange coordinates, which breaks framing and continuity.\n\n## Proposal\n\nProvide a command to place my camera at the exact position, rotation, and FOV of another user’s active camera.\n\n## Suggested UX\n\n- User Quick Menu → Select User → Camera → Match Camera -Position\n\n- Options:\n\n  - Include rotation ✔︎/✖︎\n\n  - Include FOV ✔︎/✖︎\n\n  - One-time snap or follow mode (continuous sync until toggled off)\n\nRules and Permissions\n\n- Target must have an active, shareable camera.\n\n- Consent toggle on the target side: “Allow others to match my camera.”\n\n- Respect privacy/visibility settings and world permissions.\n\n- World creators can disable this feature per world.\n\n## Why This Matters\n\n- Faster multi-camera setup for events and shoots.\n\n- Consistent framing across users for recordings and streams.\n\n- Reduces coordination overhead and misaligned shots.",
